course: dictionary
lesson: 3162
title: Emollient: soft skin and calm words
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Emollient has two meanings, and the clues around it tell you which one is meant. Look at the words near it. «Thick moisturisers called emollients every day...» The words moisturisers and eczema are clues: this is a cream for skin.
explain: The second meaning is about words and behaviour. An emollient tone in a speech is calm and gentle, so people do not get angry. Ask yourself what would fit here, then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Doctors treat eczema with emollients every day and steroid creams for flare-ups, the times when it gets worse.» The sentence explains flare-ups for you. Context clues often sit right next to a hard word, so read on before you give up.
fact: An emollient is a cream or lotion that makes dry skin soft and smooth.
fact: Doctors use emollients every day to keep eczema calm.
fact: Eczema is a skin problem, and emollients help to keep it calm.
fact: In formal writing, an emollient word or behaviour is calm and gentle, meant to stop people getting angry.
fact: Phrases to know: «emollient cream» (for skin) and «an emollient tone» (a calm, gentle way of speaking).
exercise: «Thick moisturisers called emollients every day...» What is an emollient in this sentence? | A kind of cream for dry skin | *A cream or lotion that makes dry skin soft and smooth | A rainy day in Scotland | A loud, angry shout
exercise: Mum says the speech had an emollient tone. What does it mean? | Dry and dusty | Long and boring | *Calm and gentle, so people do not get angry | Loud and angry
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Doctors treat eczema with emollients every day and steroid creams for flare-ups, the times when it gets worse.» that means the times when eczema gets worse. | emollients | *flare-ups | doctors | creams
test: What does «emollient» mean in a health lesson? | *A cream or lotion that makes dry skin soft and smooth | A sharp tool for cutting | A cold drink for hot days | A loud noise
test: «He spoke in an emollient tone, so the crowd calmed down.» What does emollient suggest here? | Loud and angry | Very fast | Wet and cold | *Calm and gentle
exam: Using context clues, which meaning of emollient fits a chemist label that says apply to dry skin? | Something that is very old | A type of bird | A calm, gentle way of speaking | *A cream or lotion for soft, smooth skin
